SDLC: Branches

Purpose:
  Software Development Life Cycle branch standards.
  Defines main, stage, test branch roles and promotion rules.

Branches:
  main:
    purpose: Production-ready code
    protection: required
    promotion: stage -> main
    merge_strategy: squash
    required_checks:
      - all gates passed
      - security scan clean
      - documentation updated

  stage:
    purpose: Pre-production integration
    protection: required
    promotion: test -> stage -> main
    merge_strategy: squash
    required_checks:
      - all tests pass
      - integration tests pass
      - performance tests pass

  test:
    purpose: Test environment deployment
    protection: optional
    promotion: test -> stage
    merge_strategy: merge
    required_checks:
      - unit tests pass
      - integration tests pass

Rules:
  [SDLC1] No direct push to main or stage — pull request only.
  [SDLC2] All required checks MUST pass before merge.
  [SDLC3] Merge strategy is squash for main and stage.
  [SDLC4] Documentation MUST be updated before merge to main.
  [SDLC5] Security scan MUST pass before merge to main.
  [SDLC6] Rollback plan MUST exist before merge to main.

State: +
